id: R07
target: src/sello/ristretto.nim
desc: ristrettoEncode: final sign-correction select inverted, 'feCMove(y, negY, feIsNegative(xZinv))' -> 'feCMove(y, negY, not feIsNegative(xZinv))' -- negates y exactly when x*z_inv is already nonnegative and leaves it alone exactly when negation is required, producing the wrong-sign encoding for every non-degenerate point. RFC-004 slice 8b's "encode's ... negation condition flip" target.
====OLD====
  feCMove(y, negY, feIsNegative(xZinv))
====NEW====
  feCMove(y, negY, not feIsNegative(xZinv))
====END====
